comments.content:
[medium] `item.data.recipientID` is interpolated into the jobId string without optional chaining or any validation. If recipientID can be null/undefined, ids such as `abc/undefined` would be produced, breaking removal/dedup and complicating debugging. Consider validating the required fields for NOTIFY_ALBUM_UPDATE (and throwing/guarding accordingly), or appending recipientID only when it is present.

```suggestion
        if (!item.data?.id || !item.data?.recipientID) {
                  throw new ImmichStartupError('NOTIFY_ALBUM_UPDATE requires id and recipientID');
                }
                return {
                  jobId: `${item.data.id}/${item.data.recipientID}`,
                  delay: item.data?.delay,
                };
```
